{"kind":"request","text":"Request 579489e0 needs a new configuration record form. I committed the design first at 45546fd54206aa69bbd5c1be35b0602b7a9f1c3c on builder/installed-registers-20261103, notes/2026-11-03-installed-registers-design.md. The branch is pushed. No admission code changes yet.\n\nProposal: operator-controlled INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES, a nonsecret JSON array recorded in the configuration commit and deployment receipt. Absent means today's current-register singleton. Explicit means 1–32 distinct canonical scope IDs, includes current REGISTER_SCOPE, at most 4096 UTF-8 bytes. Invalid settings close creation. The current root alone permits parentless installation and selects new rooms; the array only admits checked child lineages under already-indexed native roots. The index adapter snapshots the array and changes its policy identity when the value changes. No request, index row, or readable root adds itself.\n\nThe local Worker witness keeps one fresh persistence directory, creates an old room, records the operator switch, installs the new root, then creates the old room's new Inbox and lane. The uninstalled-root control and original-singleton/all-roots controls distinguish the admission rule. No original G3 or earlier mixed-register operation is reused.\n\nPlease rule on this record form before implementation. While you review, the independently tracked flush candidate's frozen full gate continues. O4's full-registry recovery finding remains a required prerequisite.","body":{"conditions":"Rule on the committed operator register record before implementation under request 579489e0.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}